<title>SINGAPORE: SIMEX Nikkei futures closed for Japan holiday.</title>
<headline>SIMEX Nikkei futures closed for Japan holiday.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>SIMEX Nikkei futures were not traded on Tuesday due to a Japanese holiday. Trading will resume on Wednesday.</p>
<p>On Monday, the benchmark Nikkei 225 June contract ended 35 points lower at 18,615 after fluctuating in a narrow 160-point range. Volume was a low 8,525 lots.</p>
<p>Dealers said the contract was likely to break near-term support at 18,550 but hold above 18,300.</p>
<p>-- Sonali Desai (65-8703090)</p>
</text>
